WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's just always
a delight to see you.

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:03.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were here 10 months ago.
-Yes.

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:04.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And a very
surreal thing happened,

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is,
the day you were here,

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
police apprehended
a suspect in the Golden --

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:11.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Golden State Killer,
basically.

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:13.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They caught
the Golden State Killer.

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:17.717
-And your -- your late wife
had written a book about him.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:21.521
-Yes.
-I was actually on a book tour.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:25.458
It was the -- we were
in Chicago, my wife's hometown,

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:29.062 size:84% position:42%
and we did the reading,
and then went to bed.

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:31.398 line:92%
And at 4:00 a.m., my phone --

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:33.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everyone's phone
started pinging,

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:33.900 line:92%
and we all met in the lobby.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we're like,
"He's been caught, I think."

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:40.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, I was coming to do
your show that night,

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.207 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and I'm on the plane.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:44.711
I think I sent
an Instagram little selfie film,

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:47.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
going, "Well,
I'm gonna go on 'Seth Meyers.'

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:51.484
I think they just caught this
killer my wife was track--"

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:53.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I didn't know
what the panel was saying,

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.622
'cause I was there to tell jokes
and promote a show,

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:58.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
and suddenly,
"We've caught a killer."

00:00:58.792 --> 00:00:59.526 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was just weird.

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:00.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know
how to segue into that.

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:04.130
So it was a very, very --
And when I was on the show,

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:07.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you watch that episode,
you can see how sleep-deprived

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
and freaked out I was.
-Yeah.

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
-'Cause I didn't --
I didn't know where --

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you were, like,
"What are we gonna talk about?

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:15.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do we approach this?"
-Yeah.

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:17.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was very interesting.
-Yes.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:20.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I --
It's nice now to have you --

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:21.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
How have
the last 10 months been?

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:23.249
I mean,
has it continued to be surreal?

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:25.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's been --
well, weirdly enough, today,

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:27.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
as we're talking,
this is the day

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:30.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the paperback
release of the book.

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:34.694
And I wrote a new afterward
that describes that day.

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.463 line:92%
And it ends on this show,

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:38.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
talking about
what I was just talking about,

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:41.868 size:84% position:42%
which was, "How do I do
a segment about a --"

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:44.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, that's not --
That's not what a comedian

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:45.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
normally does
on his talk-show segments.

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:47.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It's talking about --

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I get mentioned
in the paperback?

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:54.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Um...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:56.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
All right.
You know, it's weird.

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:58.251 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
There was, uh...

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:00.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think your lawyers
didn't want you in there.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
-So we had to...

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:03.423 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:05.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You just had a birthday.
You turned 50.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:07.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations.
-I just turned 50.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-How is it?

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:11.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
It's really --

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:13.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, no.
Oh, no.

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:16.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, no.
[ Laughing ]

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:18.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not even waving.
-It's, um...

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:20.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
I don't mind turning 50.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:23.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
What I mind is turning 50
in 2019.

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:23.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-That stinks.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:27.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because the time to turn 50
was in the '50s.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-Because people were okay

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:31.684
with you going, "Oh, you're 50.
You've had a kid.

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, you just sit down
and start to die.

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:36.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just relax,
do a crossword puzzle,

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:38.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
slowly become racist,
and then die."

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:39.392 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:43.163
But in 2019, you turn 50,
and people are like, "You're 50?

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:45.532
Well, get on your mountain bike,
you silver fox.

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:47.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's get going!"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:48.268 size:75% position:38% line:92%
"You've got decades.

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:51.337 size:81% position:41%
We've got goji berries
and alkaline water."

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:53.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
For my birthday --
At my birthday party,

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:57.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
my wife gave me
a mountain bike with --

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:58.178 size:88% position:44% line:92%
She made a poster going,

00:02:58.178 --> 00:03:00.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Here's your mountain bike,
you silver fox."

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:03.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now I am a --
I'm riding my bike around,

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is not a good look.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:07.487 line:92%
I mean, I don't really have --

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:10.356 size:75% position:38%
I look like somebody
shaved a baby panda

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:14.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
and put biking clothes on him,
and I'm just kind of --

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:17.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
There should be
carnival music playing

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
while I ride my bike around.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:21.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's what it looks like.
So, yeah.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm biking now.
God help me.

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:25.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
-God love ya.
-Thank you.

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:27.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The clip for "A.P. Bio" --
Full disclosure --

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm one of the many producers
on this show.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:33.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And thank you for -- yeah.
-I love watching it.

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:35.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Paula Pell,
one of your co-stars --

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:36.149 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Good God.

00:03:36.149 --> 00:03:37.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One of the funniest people
in the world.

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:40.887 size:75% position:38%
-Paula Pell is maybe
the funniest person

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:42.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've ever hung out with
in that --

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:43.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause she's
a brilliant actress,

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:47.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
she's a great writer,
and doing scenes with her,

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:50.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
she will riff --
constantly riff new lines

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:51.331 line:92%
at the end of the scene --

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:53.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know when
they're coming in --

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:55.368 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and always busts me up.

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:56.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
Always --
That whole thing with the --

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were just supposed
to fist bump,

00:03:58.104 --> 00:04:00.073
and then she just started going,
"Oh, I'll catch her."

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
She did that weird --

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:03.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I kind of
don't know what to do.

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:06.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then,
there was one thing she said.

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:10.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a --
Wait a minute.

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
She riffed this thing.
I can't repeat it,

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:14.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause it's so atrocious
and filthy.

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:15.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
It involved --

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:19.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
It involved
her breasts and syrup that --

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:22.762
She was at a pancake breakfast,
and it's insane.

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:23.529 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:24.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
But she added it
at the end of the scene.

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:26.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
And instead of me
just immediately cracking up,

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:28.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause they can go,
"Cut, let's do it again,"

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:31.137 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I stupidly was like,

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:33.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm gonna keep it together
and finish this scene."

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.541 line:92%
But then I'm doing that weird

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:37.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
kind of talking
when I'm choking.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:41.614
So, it looks like
I'm having a stroke, basically,

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:42.749 line:92%
while I'm talking to her.

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:46.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then it went way longer.
She is so funny.

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:47.120 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And they give her --

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
The writers give her
the weirdest stuff to do.

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:50.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, she always...
-Yeah.

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:52.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...amps it up
to an even better level.

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:54.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I --
You and Lorne making sure

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:58.398
that Mike O'Brien's writing
stays as weird as it does...

00:04:58.398 --> 00:05:00.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You just stay out of the way.
-How do you guys just --

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:01.100 line:92%
-You just stay out of the way.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.435 size:81% position:41%
I mean, Mike O'Brien
is truly one of the --

00:05:02.435 --> 00:05:04.704
He's such a great creator,
and it's a wonderful show,

00:05:04.704 --> 00:05:07.674 size:75% position:38%
and I'm very excited
for it to come back.

